    display:
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4f12abf2b49167f45b7f0df2a1e8cdc0, type: 3}
    titleName: POWER SUPPLY UNIT (PSU)
    description: A Power Supply in a computer is a hardware component that provides
      electrical power to the other components in the computer. It converts AC power
      from your wall outlet into DC power that can be used by the computer's components.
      The power supply typically has several connectors that provide power to the
      motherboard, CPU, graphics card, drives, and other components in the computer.
    has3dView: 1
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display:
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5fe83ac6dc90ed042889f9a47ff58e7f, type: 3}
    titleName: 
    description: 'Attached are vital hardware cables and buses for transferring power
      to various components in the computer. '
    has3dView: 1
  - contentName: 0
    modelName: 0
    display:
    - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 39d9593dcf3b83e44ac4c57756740905, type: 3}
    titleName: 
    description: " While most power supply units (PSUs) follow standardized designs
      for easy installation, there are specific variations suited for different purposes.\r\n
      \r\n\xB7         ATX 24 pin main power connector is the standard motherboard
      power connector used in nearly every computer.\r\n\xB7         SATA 15 pin
      power supply connector is one of several standard peripheral power connectors.
      SATA power connectors only connect to SATA drives like hard drives and optical
      drives. SATA power connectors do not work with older PATA devices.\r\n\xB7        
      Molex 4 pin power supply connector is a standard peripheral power connector.
      Molex power connectors connect to many different kinds of internal peripherals
      including PATA hard drives and optical drives, some video cards, and even some
      other devices.\r\n\xB7         Floppy drive 4 pin power supply connector is
      the standard floppy drive power connector. The floppy power connector, also
      called a Berg connector or Mini-Molex connector, is included in even the newest
      power supplies even though floppy drives are becoming obsolete.\r\n\xB7        
      ATX 4 pin power supply connector is a standard motherboard power connector
      used to provide +12 VDC to the processor voltage regulator. This small connector
      usually attaches to the motherboard near the CPU.\r\n\xB7         ATX 6 pin
      power supply connector is a motherboard power connector used to provide +12
      VDC to the processor voltage regulator but the 4-pin variety is the more commonly
      used connector. This small connector usually attaches to the motherboard near
      the CPU.\r\n"
    has3dView: 1
